   "Heihaian_main_1_3_9_4": "Welcome home.",
   "HelpText_100_Content": "[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 17 and complete \"Ominous Star.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. Participate in By Moon's Grace and help prepare for the Moonlit Fair to boost the festival's Popularity.\n2. Increase Popularity by fulfilling Wishes and building stalls.\n3. Meet the Popularity goals to claim the corresponding rewards.\n4. Any unclaimed rewards will be sent by mail upon your first login within 30 days after the event ends.",
   "HelpText_100_Title": "Converging Paths",
-  "HelpText_101_Content": "1. During the Moon-Chasing Festival, you can increase Popularity via the activities in <color=#8c7e51>Lodge Wishes</color> and <color=#8c7e51>Fair Stalls</color> to make the Moonlit Fair more lively.\n2. Popularity ranges from Level 1 to Level 6.",
+  "HelpText_101_Content": "1. During the Moon-Chasing Festival, you can increase Popularity via the activities in <color=#8c7e51>Lodge Wishes</color> and <color=#8c7e51>Fair Stalls</color> to make the Moonlit Fair more lively.\n2. Popularity starts from Level 1 and can reach as high as Level 6.",
   "HelpText_101_Title": "Popularity",
   "HelpText_102_Content": "1. Build or upgrade stalls to increase Popularity, gain buffs, and unlock Companions.\n2. Building or upgrading stalls requires Funds, which can be earned by completing Wishes in Lodge Wishes.\n3. Stalls can be upgraded multiple times, with higher levels providing greater buffs.\n4. After building a stall, you can participate in the stall's activities and may earn unexpected rewards, with additional daily rewards for Thus Says the Moon, Hsin's Fortuity, and Riddle Twiddle.",
   "HelpText_102_Title": "Fair Stalls",
@@ -97062,7 +97173,7 @@
   "InfoDisplay_120101002_Title": "Huaxu Hive",
   "InfoDisplay_120101004_Text": "To the Moontree Lodge,\n \nThey say that Moon-Chasing Festival is a time for family reunions, but my son is no longer here. The house feels so empty without him. I miss the old days, with him by my side, the both of us together, sharing conversation... Is he as lonely in that other world as I am in this one? Should I go be with him? But I promised that I'd live a long, full life and take care of myself... Oh, Moontree Lodge, I've gotten so old, what do I have to wish for anymore? If you really can pull off miracles as they say, please, tell me. What should I do?\n\nHeying",
   "InfoDisplay_120101004_Title": "Heying's Wish",
-  "InfoDisplay_120101006_Text": "Almighty Moontree Lodge,\n\nI have a secret to tell you.\nShhh—I might have awakened my incredible abilities like the heroes in hero plays.\nWell... I'm saying this because... I could only eat one bowl of rice for lunch in the past, but now I can finish two large bowls! Also, I used to have to step on a small bench to touch the branches of Grandpa Tree, but now I only need to jump casually to touch them!\nI feel like something amazing is burning inside my body. Is this what it feels like to become a great hero? I've been waiting for ages now. I wonder when I'll be able to use amazing powers like Blaze Ranger...\nMoontree Lodge, oh Moontree Lodge, the adults all say that you can make any wish come true... Can you help me become a great hero?\n\nMahn",
+  "InfoDisplay_120101006_Text": "Almighty Moontree Lodge,\n\nI have a secret to tell you.\nShhh—I might have awakened my incredible abilities like the heroes in hero plays.\nWell... I'm saying this because... I could only eat one bowl of rice for lunch in the past, but now I can finish two large bowls! Also, I used to have to step on a small bench to touch the branches of Grandpa Tree, but now I only need to jump casually to touch them!\nI feel like something amazing is burning inside my body. Is this what it feels like to become a great hero? I've been waiting for ages now. I wonder when I'll be able to use amazing powers like Flame Ranger...\nMoontree Lodge, oh Moontree Lodge, the adults all say that you can make any wish come true... Can you help me become a great hero?\n\nMahn",
   "InfoDisplay_120101006_Title": "Mahn's Wish",
   "InfoDisplay_120101011_Text": "When \"the Genius\" Meets \"the Ordinary\": An Exclusive Interview with the Mysterious Polymath\n\nQ: This is your first time speaking to the public, right? Are you nervous? Everyone's been so curious about what the legendary \"genius\" is like.\nA: Haha, actually, I've interacted with many of you on various topics without you even realizing it. Maybe you would recall discussing proton lifetime with someone named Cream Cat.\n\nQ: That science writer Cream Cat? So it's also you! What a surprise! By the way, does this pseudonym have any special meaning?\nA: It's from a little \"aha\" moment. Let me ask you this: ever accidentally dropped a cream cake? If you have, you've probably noticed the creamy side always hits the ground first, just like a cat always lands on its paws. Now, imagine this: stick the non-creamed side onto a cat's back, and voilà! You've got yourself a cream-cat perpetual motion machine, spinning 24/7—a true scientific marvel.\n\nQ: It must take a whimsical and creative mind to come up with such an interesting idea. I wonder if your research on Automata Mechanics is just as imaginative.\nA: To answer that, let's raise our heads and look at the starry sky through the window above. What do you see at first glance? And if you look further, what do you see next?\n\nQ: First, the moon and stars. Beyond that, maybe planets crashing into each other or the starry sky mirroring the world we live in.\nA: Now, are these just your imagination or scientific facts waiting to be confirmed? You can't find the answer if you don't imagine it first, right? It's the same with my research: imagination is part of scientification. Researchers today often focus too much on the utilitarian side of science, abandoning imagination to ensure their work contributes to mankind and the world as a whole, even if it goes against their intuition. Applied research is undoubtedly necessary for post-Lament reconstruction, but that's no reason to give up imagination, the breeding ground of science. So, my advice is... just think about how to make the science work. As for what it might yield, well... (smiles)\n\nQ: How enlightening! Speaking of advice, do you have any for your gifted son, Xiangli Yao? As a genius yourself, you must have high expectations for him.\nA: That might be a lot for a young boy to handle, <color=Highlight>but... I just hope he inherits my way of seeing things. So that one day, when he steps out of his room and tries to make sense of this world, he can look up at the sky and find the answers there.</color>",
   "InfoDisplay_120101011_Title": "Shabby Journal",
